708
02:34:01,040 --> 02:34:21,680
I think maybe the biggest danger of AI and robotics going wrong is government. People who are opposed to corporations or worried about corporations should

709
02:34:21,680 --> 02:34:30,479
really worry the most about government. Because government is just a corporation in the limit. Government is just the biggest

710
02:34:30,479 --> 02:34:41,680
corporation with a monopoly on violence. I always find it a strange dichotomy where people would think corporations are bad, but the government is good, when the government is

711
02:34:41,680 --> 02:34:55,840
simply the biggest and worst corporation. But people have that dichotomy. They somehow think at the same time that government can be good, but corporations bad, and this is not true.

712
02:34:55,840 --> 02:35:12,720
Corporations have better morality than the government. I actually think it’s a thing to be worried about. The government could potentially use AI and

713
02:35:12,720 --> 02:35:28,560
robotics to suppress the population. That is a serious concern. As the guy building AI and robotics, how do you prevent that?

714
02:35:28,560 --> 02:35:37,760
If you limit the powers of government, which is really what the US Constitution is intended to do, to limit the powers of government, then you're probably going to have a better outcome than

715
02:35:37,760 --> 02:35:49,840
if you have more government. Robotics will be available to all governments, right? I don’t know about all governments.

716
02:35:49,840 --> 02:36:08,800
It's difficult to predict. I can say what's the endpoint, or what is many years in the future, but it's difficult to predict the path along that way. If civilization progresses, AI will vastly

717
02:36:08,800 --> 02:36:20,720
exceed the sum of all human intelligence. There will be far more robots than humans. Along the way what happens is very difficult to predict.

718
02:36:20,720 --> 02:36:31,439
It seems one thing you could do is just say, "whatever government X, you're not allowed to use Optimus to do X, Y, Z." Just write out a policy. I think you tweeted recently that

719
02:36:31,439 --> 02:36:47,439
Grok should have a moral constitution. One of those things could be that we limit what governments are allowed to do with this advanced technology.

720
02:36:47,439 --> 02:37:01,040
Technically if politicians pass a law and they can enforce that law, then it's hard to not do that law. The best thing we can have is limited government

721
02:37:01,040 --> 02:37:17,359
where you have the appropriate crosschecks between the executive, judicial, and legislative branches. The reason I'm curious about it is that at some point it seems the limits will come from you.

722
02:37:17,359 --> 02:37:32,479
You've got the Optimus, you've got the space GPUs… You think I'll be the boss of the government? Already it's the case with SpaceX that for things that are crucial—the government really

723
02:37:32,479 --> 02:37:44,960
cares about getting certain satellites up in space or whatever—it needs SpaceX. It is the necessary contractor. You are in the process of building more and more of the

724
02:37:44,960 --> 02:37:58,560
technological components of the future that will have an analogous role in different industries. You could have this ability to set some policy that suppressing classical liberalism in any

725
02:37:58,560 --> 02:38:08,640
way… "My companies will not help in any way with that", or some policy like that. I will do my best to ensure that anything that's within my control

726
02:38:08,640 --> 02:38:29,040
